;; kawaraban 瓦版 — live-ingest outlet allowlist (ADR-2607110200, R0->R1).
;;
;; G4 invariant: every entry MUST be :access :open (or :registration-wall) — never
;; :paywall / :proprietary-terminal (ingest.cljc / outlet_ingest cell refuse those anyway;
;; this file only lists candidates that are ALREADY public-facing by policy, not just by
;; the runtime gate).
;;
;; Selection criterion (owner instruction 2026-07-10): state/public-broadcaster or
;; non-profit/international-organization press ONLY — no commercial/ad-funded outlets.
;;
;; :verified / :note ARE MACHINE-OWNED — DO NOT HAND-EDIT (ADR-2607252600, 2026-07-25).
;;
;; :verified true  — this exact :feed-url actually returned HTTP 200 with parseable
;;                    RSS/Atom items on the date recorded in its :note. A measurement,
;;                    not a confidence level.
;; :verified false — could not be confirmed on that date; :note says why (404, an HTML
;;                    landing page, 403 bot-block, unreachable, or 0 items). The entry is
;;                    KEPT rather than deleted so that "tried and could not collect" stays
;;                    distinguishable from "never considered" — the orchestrator filters on
;;                    :verified, so an unverified entry is inert, not harmful.
;;
;; Both fields are written by:
;;   nbb scripts/verify-feeds.cljs data/outlets/allowlist.edn --discover --apply
;; which re-measures every feed and, for entries whose URL is missing or dead, discovers a
;; replacement from the outlet's homepage <link rel="alternate"> (or common feed paths).
;; The prior convention was a hand-written "well-known, high-confidence endpoint" flag; on
;; 2026-07-25 that flag claimed 30 working feeds when only 29 actually parsed, which is why
;; the judgement moved out of human memory and into a re-runnable measurement (G5).
;;
;; Adding an outlet: append :id/:name/:kind/:country/:lang/:access/:homepage/:section
;; (:feed-url optional — discovery will look for it), run verify-feeds.cljs --discover
;; --apply, then add a matching :news.outlet/* record via the outlet_ingest cell
;; (data/lex/outlet.edn) before it can appear in a :mirror article.

